4019-/// 0.8.20 Slice 15d (R-20-PR) — the diff [`Engine::configure_projections`]
4020-/// applied. Idempotent re-registration yields `unchanged == true` with all
4021-/// vecs empty (the "re-registration is a no-op" acceptance signal). A
4022-/// destructive change without an explicit `drop` is an `Err`, not a delta.
4023-#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default, Eq, PartialEq)]
4024-pub struct ProjectionDelta {
4025-    /// Attribute names whose same-transaction projections (EAV / property-FTS)
4026-    /// were (re)built by this apply.
4027-    pub built: Vec<String>,
4028-    /// Attribute names dropped (explicit `drop` list) — their EAV + property-FTS
4029-    /// rows and registry row removed.
4030-    pub dropped: Vec<String>,
4031-    /// Attribute names whose declared roles were persisted but NOT built:
4032-    /// `rankable` (F9 not yet live) and the `searchable→vector` sub-target
4033-    /// (Slice 20). These graft on a future idempotent apply. No error.
4034-    pub deferred: Vec<String>,
4035-    /// True iff nothing was built, dropped, or newly deferred — the whole apply
4036-    /// diffed to a no-op.
4037-    pub unchanged: bool,
4038-    /// 0.8.20 Slice 22 (R-20-VC / **TC-67**) — **node KINDS, not attribute
4039-    /// names.** The vector-eligible node kinds present in the corpus that the
4040-    /// vector writer can NEVER commit, so no `searchable→vector` declaration
4041-    /// will ever produce an embedding for them.
4042-    ///
4043-    /// # Why this field exists — the silence it replaces
4044-    ///
4045-    /// [`kind_is_vector_committable`] (Slice 20c fix-2) restricted enrolment to
4046-    /// the kinds [`resolve_source_type`] maps, because enrolling any other kind
4047-    /// is a permanent liveness wedge. That fix was correct and is unchanged —
4048-    /// but it made the exclusion **silent**: the declaration persists, its name
4049-    /// is pushed onto [`ProjectionDelta::deferred`], and the caller cannot tell
4050-    /// "waiting on the embedder" (transient) from "this kind will never be
4051-    /// embedded" (permanent). Per the HITL ruling on TC-67 the remedy is
4052-    /// option **(c) REPORT** — the vocabulary is NOT grown and the Pack-1 D3
4053-    /// partition-key lock is NOT touched (`dev/design/0.7.0-vector-quant-pack1.md`).
4054-    ///
4055-    /// # Axis, and why the name is what it is
4056-    ///
4057-    /// `built` / `dropped` / `deferred` are all lists of **projection attribute
4058-    /// names**. This one is a list of **node kinds** — a different axis entirely,
4059-    /// so the name says `kinds` explicitly and is prefixed `vector_` to bind it
4060-    /// to the dense arm (an unsupported kind is still fully FTS/lexically
4061-    /// searchable). Sorted and de-duplicated (`SELECT DISTINCT … ORDER BY kind`).
4062-    ///
4063-    /// # It is a STATE report, not a diff
4064-    ///
4065-    /// Unlike the other three vectors it does not describe what this call
4066-    /// changed; it describes the corpus as it stands. So it is populated on an
4067-    /// idempotent re-apply too (where `unchanged == true` and the other three
4068-    /// are empty), and it deliberately does NOT feed [`ProjectionDelta::unchanged`].
4069-    /// That is what makes the declare-time residual cheap to live with: to
4070-    /// refresh the report after writing new kinds, re-apply the same spec — a
4071-    /// no-op that still returns a current report.
4072-    ///
4073-    /// # Independent of the embedder
4074-    ///
4075-    /// Computed whenever a `searchable→vector` projection is declared, whether
4076-    /// or not this session has a live embedder. The vocabulary is static, so
4077-    /// "this kind can never be embedded" is true in a no-embedder session too —
4078-    /// and must not be conflated with the Q6a graceful-absent deferral, which is
4079-    /// transient and is reported through `deferred`.
4080-    ///
4081-    /// Empty (never absent) when there is nothing to report.
4082-    pub vector_unsupported_kinds: Vec<String>,

